      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{6161a61a2c0de966b4e43486|full_name}: Yesss finally :D I don't use mods, but when this is solved better all my desires to use them are gone!\nMight want to merge this with this post: https://feedback.vrchat.com/vrchat-ik-20/p/stop-locking-avatars-in-place-when-players-walk-through-walls\nAlso i just had another idea how to potentially improve it: Maybe you could make a \"pose mode\" that you can manually enable, where your tracking doesnt die when you \"enter\" a collider. However, it also disables your ability to enter stations or interact with any other object (except camera). That way you could take nice pictures at places otherwise inconvenient or inaccessible, while still being unable to \"cheat\" or something like that.\nBest solution in my head is to make it an option for world creators \"allow/disallow tracking through walls\", being allowed by default. That way creators with puzzles/games can disable it to deny cheaters, and the default pretty world allows for convenient behavior.",
